WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.202
Week four, with Brent Smart, former CMO of Telstra and IAG.

00:00:05.252 --> 00:00:06.052
Marketing is a battle for memory,

00:00:05.948 --> 00:00:09.850
and the biggest risk is taking no risk.

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:13.300
You're competing with how people spend their time.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:18.237
And categories look identical: bottled water is always an alpine stream.

00:00:18.933 --> 00:00:23.305
Liquid Death broke every code and became the fastest-growing water brand in the world.

00:00:23.355 --> 00:00:26.029
Great ideas often sound stupid at first.

00:00:26.079 --> 00:00:27.875
That's the signal.

00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:33.788
Creative work returns two and a half times the revenue growth and four times the profit of the average ad.

00:00:33.838 --> 00:00:36.813
Dull costs twenty and a half million extra.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.313
He's proved it three times.

00:00:39.363 --> 00:00:42.367
Yellow Pages' treehouse used zero paid media.

00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:44.455
Cheerios rode out a backlash.

00:00:44.505 --> 00:00:47.834
NRMA's koalas went from thirty-sixth to fifth.

00:00:48.533 --> 00:00:50.570
If it's not bold, it's dumb.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:52.870
Bad ideas are safe and comfortable.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:57.547
Good ones feel uncomfortable, and with no data, conviction does the work.

00:00:58.233 --> 00:01:01.343
Telstra's reputation sat barely above the tax office.

00:01:01.393 --> 00:01:02.770
Asked to draw the brand,

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.008
people drew a suit,

00:01:04.058 --> 00:01:05.011
the Monopoly man,

00:01:05.061 --> 00:01:06.359
a bully.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:09.717
Only fifteen percent of buyers are in market now,

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:11.439
ready for logic and offers.

00:01:11.489 --> 00:01:15.553
The other eighty-five percent need emotion, memories for later.

00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:19.024
Don't just talk to the four hands that are up right now.

00:01:19.074 --> 00:01:22.857
Someone buying a phone in three years is worth reaching today.

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:26.335
Activation spikes, then drops when you stop.

00:01:26.385 --> 00:01:28.470
Brand building rises slowly.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:30.828
The benchmark is sixty percent brand.

00:01:30.878 --> 00:01:34.405
Telstra was at twenty, so he went to fifty first.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.067
Be a magnet, not a mirror.

00:01:37.117 --> 00:01:41.288
Put a still from your ad, logo removed, beside three rivals.

00:01:41.338 --> 00:01:44.786
If nobody can tell which is yours, it's a mirror.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.702
Telstra made twenty-six stop-motion ads,

00:01:47.752 --> 00:01:50.037
each an Australian animal in a real place,

00:01:50.087 --> 00:01:52.926
with forty-two local voices and handmade puppets.

00:01:52.976 --> 00:01:55.042
It won a Grand Prix.

00:01:55.733 --> 00:01:59.221
The brand on one page: a connected future for everyone.

00:01:59.271 --> 00:02:01.803
Positioning, engineering possibility.

00:02:01.853 --> 00:02:04.044
The platform, wherever we go.

00:02:04.094 --> 00:02:06.811
Always crafted with a human hand.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:11.129
The whistling ad used animation, no phones and metaphor.

00:02:11.179 --> 00:02:13.252
At launch, people hated it.

00:02:13.302 --> 00:02:17.186
But being noticed beats being liked, so he held his nerve.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:20.150
Then people started copying the walk.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.355
Thirty million organic TikTok views,

00:02:22.405 --> 00:02:23.687
zero paid spend,

00:02:23.737 --> 00:02:26.458
and Telstra credited the people who made them.

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:29.181
Even the posters were handmade.

00:02:29.231 --> 00:02:32.895
People can tell made from generated, and read effort as care.

00:02:32.945 --> 00:02:35.437
Craft is a strategic choice.

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:38.147
Marketing ROI rose from six point one to ten point four in four years,

00:02:38.197 --> 00:02:41.496
on lower spend.

00:02:41.546 --> 00:02:45.891
Even performance marketing converted better, thanks to a stronger brand.

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:50.571
With AI, content is either slop or irreplaceably human.

00:02:50.621 --> 00:02:53.755
Telstra's AI Santa took eight hundred thousand calls.

00:02:53.805 --> 00:02:56.262
But you need an idea first.

00:02:56.967 --> 00:02:58.497
So make the brand memorable,

00:02:58.547 --> 00:02:59.794
build future demand,

00:02:59.844 --> 00:03:01.693
and craft it with a human hand.

00:03:01.743 --> 00:03:04.853
Creativity thrives on kindness, so be kind.

00:03:04.903 --> 00:03:07.229
That's week four.
